@subsection lloptions.h

Functions for handling for (opaque) string & numeric options.
Options are fetched on-the-fly when requested, in the following order:
@itemize
@item First from report properties (if getdeoptstr_rpt or getoptint_rpt),
@item then from db properties
@item then from global properties
@item then from fallback properties.
@end itemize
3
@subsubsection Initialization & Termination

@defun get_db_options (HashTable *opts) @arrow{} void
@defunx set_db_options (HashTable *opts) @arrow{} void
In Lifelines, there was the option to store options in special records
in the database.  The options were retrieved at startup (via
@code{get_db_options} and stored after any user edit of them (via
@code{set_db_options}.

In DeadEnds, the database is created at startup from
the @code{GEDCOM} file.  DeadEnds does not currently allow the user
the option to specify database specific options.

While there are no plans to add this capability in the future, it has
not been ruled ouyt.  If it is added, what form it will take has not
been decided.
@end defun

@defun set_cmd_options (HashTable *opts) @arrow{} void
Used to set options specified on the command line.
@end defun

@defun setoptstr_fallback (String optname, String newval) @arrow{} void
Sets a fallback value for the specified option.

In the Lifelines port, it is currently called to set a fallback value
for the options:
@*Parameters:
@itemize
@item @code{DEPROGRAMS}
@item @code{DEREPORTS}
@item @code{DEARCHIVES}
@item @code{DEDATABASES}
@item @code{DEEDITOR}
@end itemize
If the option is not found in the other option locations, then the
fallback location is searched.
@end defun

@defun load_global_options (String configfile, String * pmsg) @arrow{} int
Part of initialization.  Loads the configuration file
@code{configfile}.

Returns @code{1} for ok, @code{0} for not found, and @code{-1} for
error.  In the event of failure, it sets @code{pmsg} with a message
describing the problem.
@end defun

@defun register_notify (CALLBACK_FNC fncptr) @arrow{} void
Register a function to be called when options change.
@end defun
@defun unregister_notify (CALLBACK_FNC fncptr) @arrow{} void
Unregister a function previously registered to be called when options
change.
@end defun

@defun term_lloptions (void) @arrow{} void
Called by @code{close_lifelines} as part of program termination.
Frees memory allocated by the option subsystem.
@end defun

@defun free_optable (HashTable** ptab) @arrow{} void
Free the specified option table. @code{ptab}.
@end defun

@subsubsection Routine Use

All options are stored as strings.

@defun getdeoptstr (CString optname, String defval) @arrow{} String
Returns a DE option @code{optname}.  If not found, the default value
@code{defval} is returned.
@end defun

@defun getdeoptint (CString optname, int defval) @arrow{} int
Returns a DE option @code{optname}.  If not found, the default value
@code{defval} is returned.

Calls @code{getdeoptstr} and converts the results to an integer.
@end defun

@defun getdeoptstr_dbonly (CString optname, String defval) @arrow{} String
Returns the database specific option @code{optname}.

No current callers.  And no current way to set the options.
@end defun

@defun getdeoptstr_rpt (CString optname, String defval) @arrow{} String
Searches a report specific option list.  Returns the value found.  If
no value is found, then @code{defval} is returned.

Currently nothing sets any report specific options.
@end defun

@defun get_property (CString opt) @arrow{} String
Called by DE script function @code{getproperty}.  Searches a report
specific option list (by calling @code{getdeoptstr_rpt}) and if that
fails, then searches the standard option lists (by calling
@code{getdeoptstr}).

Unless you are extending an existing scripting language or are adding
a new one, you probably don't need to call this.
@end defun

